# 0704 — SERIES 700 TESTING

## LEGAiSEE COMMANDCENTER KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM

Version: 1.0
Status: ACTIVE GOVERNANCE STANDARD

---

# PURPOSE

The Testing subsystem defines the standards, methods, and governance for validating the correctness, stability, reliability, and safety of all components within the LEGAiSEE CommandCenter before they are deployed or modified in production.

Testing ensures that system behavior aligns with intended design and governance rules before operational impact occurs.

---

# CORE PRINCIPLE

Nothing enters production unverified.

Every system change must be tested against expected behavior, operational constraints, and governance requirements.

Testing is not optional validation—it is a structural requirement for system trust.

---

# OBJECTIVES

The Testing subsystem shall:

* validate system correctness
* prevent production instability
* detect defects early
* enforce governance compliance
* ensure predictable behavior
* reduce operational risk
* support continuous improvement
* verify integration integrity

---

# TESTING LEVELS

Testing is performed across multiple levels of system abstraction.

---

## Unit Testing

Validates individual functions, modules, or components in isolation.

Focus:

* correctness of logic
* expected outputs
* boundary conditions
* error handling

Unit testing ensures internal component reliability.

---

## Integration Testing

Validates interaction between multiple system components.

Focus:

* module interoperability
* data flow correctness
* engine coordination
* cross-system dependencies

Integration testing ensures system cohesion.

---

## System Testing

Validates the complete CommandCenter as a unified system.

Focus:

* end-to-end workflows
* performance under load
* operational stability
* feature completeness

System testing ensures operational readiness.

---

## Regression Testing

Ensures new changes do not break existing functionality.

Focus:

* previously validated behavior
* historical workflows
* legacy compatibility
* system consistency

Regression testing protects system stability over time.

---

## Acceptance Testing

Validates system readiness from an operator perspective.

Focus:

* usability
* workflow correctness
* expected outcomes
* operational alignment

Acceptance testing confirms real-world usability.

---

# TESTING PIPELINE

All testing follows a structured process.

```text id="704test01"
Test Planning
        │
        ▼
Test Case Design
        │
        ▼
Environment Setup
        │
        ▼
Test Execution
        │
        ▼
Result Analysis
        │
        ▼
Defect Reporting
        │
        ▼
Fix Validation
        │
        ▼
Retesting
        │
        ▼
